    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0611" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg511"/>

                <head>No. 383.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Valera.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 30,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 30th instant, in which you communicate reports of the Spanish consuls at
                    Savannah, New Orleans, and Baltimore, with reference to alleged plots against
                    the peace of Cuba, I have the honor to say that the contents thereof have been
                    made known to the Secretary of the Treasury and the Attorney General.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
